 ## Background
-The unnormalized Gaussian function is a standard representation in computer graphics, used in Early Wobble Area (EWA) splatting [ZPVBG02] and foundational to 3D Gaussian Splatting [KKLD23]. It is defined in [S1] as a Gaussian distribution where the amplitude at the mean equals the opacity.
+The unnormalized Gaussian function is defined in [S1] as a Gaussian representation used in 3D Gaussian Splatting where the amplitude at the mean equals the opacity [S1]. It serves as a standard mathematical primitive for spatial distribution modeling in splatting-based rendering pipelines [G].
 
